# Super Dodge Ball (USA) — "idle into match" input schedule.
#
# Drives the stock game from the title screen through team-select and into a
# match, then leaves the controller alone. With --ram-init zeros this run is
# deterministic frame for frame, which is what makes it the reproduction
# vector for the sprite-flicker work (docs/research.md section 2.1):
#
#   frames 865-868  object 3 (Enemy B) is emitted
#   frames 869-872  the game's per-object flag suppresses it
#   frames 873-877  emitted again
#   ...             a 9-frame cycle, 4 frames off / 5 on, forever
#
# Format: one "<frame> <BUTTONS>" line per state change, absolute state
# ("-" is release). `#` starts a comment.
0 -
11 START
14 -
21 START+RIGHT
22 -
24 B
27 -
30 A
32 -
44 A
45 -
224 DOWN
242 -
243 RIGHT
